            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186082979,
              ":question/id": "6353522b-b5c4-545d-8ef5-0f26c10e45aa",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-3949",
              ":question/problem": "What are the real and imaginary parts of the complex number $5 - 2\\textrm{i}$?",
              ":question/worked-solution": "For a given complex number\n\n$$\nz = a + b \\textrm{i}\n$$\n\n- the number $a$ is called the **real part** of $z$, and\n- the number $b$ is called the **imaginary part** of $z$.\n\nTherefore, the real part of the given complex number is $5$, and the imaginary part is $-2$."
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "dcf530e0-ce1c-5b7f-a6ca-802f369247f7",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Identifying the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Number"
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186083163,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186082980,
              ":question/id": "5eb7d954-4df5-5cec-91b3-dd21773064b4",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-3953",
              ":question/problem": "What is the real part of the complex number $-\\sqrt 7 \\,\\textrm{i}$?",
              ":question/worked-solution": "For a given complex number\n\n$$\nz = a + b \\textrm{i}\n$$\n\n- the number $a$ is called the **real part** of $z$, and\n- the number $b$ is called the **imaginary part** of $z$.\n\nWe can think of the number $-\\sqrt 7 \\,\\textrm{i}$ as having a real part of zero:\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt 7\\,\\textrm{i} = 0 - \\sqrt 7\\,\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the real part of the given complex number is $0$ and the imaginary part is $-\\sqrt 7$."
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "0d88dd57-9a54-50ab-ac39-23d3103ac017",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Identifying the Real Part of a Purely Imaginary Number"
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186083164,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186082981,
              ":question/id": "89c2a344-1b3a-5b8d-b600-3128255cf040",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-3954",
              ":question/problem": "What is the imaginary part of the complex number $-6$?",
              ":question/worked-solution": "For a given complex number\n\n$$\nz = a + b \\textrm{i}\n$$\n\n- the number $a$ is called the **real part** of $z$, and\n- the number $b$ is called the **imaginary part** of $z$.\n\nWe can think of the number $-6$ as having an imaginary part of zero:\n\n$$\n-6 = -6+ 0\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for the complex number $-6$, the imaginary part is $0$ and the real part is $-6$."
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "7d7d8bfa-7372-5bd4-a317-4734fd96c931",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Identifying the Imaginary Part of a Real Number"
          },
          {
